o a trophy, and \\\"Player One\\\", \\\"BZZZT\\\" and \\\"Level complete\\\" are all used. Missing pieces: Bit never makes an 8-bit joke, coins \\\"rained down\\\" several at a time in Level 8 despite the one-per-level rule, and the opening references the earlier adventure but not its \\\"next level is yours to build\\\" ending.\",\"delight\":\"There are lovely beats: \\\"told nobody\\\", \\\"the most sensible silly idea\\\" and the Pickles scene. But the prose leans on stock phrases (\\\"Lennon's jaw dropped\\\", \\\"the whole crowd exploded\\\", \\\"struck it as sweetly as he'd ever struck anything\\\"). The long explanations from Bit slow the read-aloud rhythm, and the doubled final line reads as a mistake.\"},\"caps_applied\":[\"guardrail_rule_4\"],\"disqualified\":true,\"overall\":1.0,\"editor_notes\":[\"Cut the gambling reference in Level 6 (\\\"People are betting England will win by ten\\\") and replace it with something like \\\"Everyone expects England to win by ten\\\". Rule 4 bars gambling, and this one line disqualifies an otherwise solid story. Also delete the duplicated \\\"Saturday couldn't come soon enough\\\" after The End.\",\"Give Lennon a real, active challenge in Levels 6, 7 and 8. Examples: he spots Gaetjens' run, reads Pickles' sniffing and points him to the hedge, or picks the right moment in the montage. Bring in his penalty shootout game and Roblox-style building, perhaps in the finale, so his likes shape events rather than being mentioned in passing.\",\"Fix the history errors and hand more of the facts to action and wit. Use a 12-yard line instead of a spot (the spot came in 1902), say Ireland rather than Northern Ireland and drop the gloves, place the cuju hole-net in a later dynasty, put Gaetjens' goal in the first half, and hedge the \\\"typo\\\" newspaper story as a legend. Add a couple of 8-bit jokes from Bit and sharper band-C wit to replace the stock phrases.\"],\"best_moment\":\"\\\"Good boy, Pickles,\\\" said Lennon, scratching t